Grove PATCH-20: complete the ZEPH/ZANO registration — the half-wired sites

Every defect this patch fixes has one shape: a coin registered in ONE HALF of
a paired site. Something enumerates coins in two places — a POST handler and
its template, a coin-set registry and a launcher gate, a base class and its
subclass — and ZEPH or ZANO was added to one of them. Each half is
individually correct, which is why source review, the type checker and the
invariant suites all passed over them; only asking "who is the partner site,
and does it agree?" finds them. Found by a dedicated sweep on 2026-09-03,
prompted by PATCH-18's own instance of the same shape (an interface built but
never wired to its dispatch site).

  interface/zano/zano.py
      ZanoInterface extends CoinInterface directly, so unlike XMR/WOW/ZEPH
      (which reach XMRInterface's copies) it inherited neither validateFeeRate
      nor findConfirmedTxnByHash -- yet basicswap.py calls both unguarded, on
      every ZANO offer creation AND on every INBOUND peer offer, where an
      AttributeError raises inside the message handler. findConfirmedTxnByHash
      is also reached from checkXmrBidState, i.e. coin-B refund detection, so
      its absence was fund-relevant rather than merely a crash.

      validateFeeRate is a deliberate no-op matching XMRInterface's.
      findConfirmedTxnByHash is built on get_recent_txs_and_info3 -- the same
      wallet-history call _getTxUnlockTimes already uses -- rather than a
      translation of XMR's incoming_transfers, which Zano has no equivalent
      for. It has NOT been exercised against a live Zano wallet: no patched
      Zano binary exists on any machine here.

  bin/run.py
      zano appeared in no branch, so it fell through to the generic Bitcoin
      launcher, which appends "-datadir=" and has no manage_wallet_daemon
      handling at all -- aborting startup before swap_client.start(). It is
      deliberately NOT added to the CryptoNote tuple: startXmrDaemon launches
      a monerod-shaped process and zanod is not one. The new branch starts
      nothing and says so if the config ever asks otherwise.

  interface/zano/core.py
      manage_daemon was ctx.should_manage_daemon("ZANO") under a comment
      asserting Grove's supervisor forces it False at runtime "the same way it
      already does for XMR/ZEPH". The supervisor did the opposite: it wrote
      manage_daemon = <coin is enabled>. Now hardcoded False here as well, so
      the engine is correct standing alone, and the supervisor was fixed
      separately (swap_sidecar.rs, HOST_MANAGED_DAEMON_COINS).

  templates/settings.html
      page_settings.py reads fee_priority_zephyr and managedaemon_zephyr
      unconditionally via get_data_entry -- a raw dict subscript -- while all
      three gates in this template still said ("wownero", "monero"). Saving
      Zephyr settings raised KeyError every single time.

  templates/wallet.html
      w.cid in "6, 9" is a SUBSTRING test on a string: "6" and "9" match,
      "16" (ZANO) and "19" (ZEPH) do not. Both fell to branches that do not
      serve them -- Subtract Fee, which the CryptoNote withdraw path ignores
      (so the wallet could not be emptied), and show_utxo_groups, whose
      handler calls ci.getUnspentsByAddr(), absent on every CryptoNote
      interface, rendering a full-page error instead of the wallet. Replaced
      with membership over an explicit id list.

  bin/prepare.py
      Two independent faults.
      (a) prepareCore looped over signers and then raised if the loop had not
          set passed -- so an EMPTY signer table raised unconditionally.
          zephyr and zano are the only two coins that publish no signer at all
          (deliberately: neither release is signed, and each module overrides
          verifyCoreSignature with a documented no-op), so both modules' own
          "clear, actionable error" paths were unreachable dead code. "No
          signers" is a different case from "every signer failed" and is now
          dispatched as one. Verified first that neither module dereferences
          signing_key_name, so a None signer is safe.
      (b) modify_tor_config gated on ("monero", "wownero"), so ZEPH and ZANO
          fell into the Bitcoin branch and hit sys.exit(1) -- ZEPH on a
          zephyr.conf that does not exist (the real file is zephyrd.conf),
          ZANO on "Unknown default onion listening port". ZEPH is a Monero
          fork and belongs in the CryptoNote branch, whose defaults already
          resolve correctly for it; ZANO is host-managed and now refuses
          explicitly, naming who should configure it instead.

Not fixed here, recorded so it is not rediscovered: ZANO is also absent from
page_settings.py's fee_priority handling, but CONSISTENTLY with its template,
so it produces Bitcoin-style fields on a CryptoNote coin rather than a crash.

Applies on top of PATCH-19.

diff --git a/basicswap/interface/zano/zano.py b/basicswap/interface/zano/zano.py
index ac81ad8..d0f8dec 100644
--- a/basicswap/interface/zano/zano.py
+++ b/basicswap/interface/zano/zano.py
@@ -815,6 +815,85 @@ class ZanoInterface(CoinInterface):
         DEFAULT_ZANO_FEE_ATOMIC = 10000000000  # 0.01 ZANO, matches REU26 rung1/2's observed fee
         return float(self.format_amount(DEFAULT_ZANO_FEE_ATOMIC)), "zano_default_fee"
 
+    def validateFeeRate(
+        self, fee_rate: int, concept_type: int, force_bypass: bool = False
+    ) -> None:
+        # PWNDA-PATCH-20: ZanoInterface extends CoinInterface directly, so unlike
+        # XMR/WOW/ZEPH (which reach XMRInterface's copy) it inherited no
+        # validateFeeRate -- yet the engine calls it unguarded on every ZANO offer
+        # creation (basicswap.py postOffer) and, worse, on every INBOUND peer offer
+        # (processOffer), where an AttributeError raises inside the message handler.
+        #
+        # Semantics match XMRInterface's: a no-op. Zano's transfer RPC takes an
+        # explicit numeric fee (see get_fee_rate above) and the scriptless leg never
+        # negotiates a rate, so there is no rate to validate. This is a deliberate
+        # no-op, not a stub -- do not "implement" it later without first establishing
+        # that a rate is actually used somewhere.
+        pass
+
+    def findConfirmedTxnByHash(self, txid: str):
+        # PWNDA-PATCH-20: second method missing for the same reason as
+        # validateFeeRate above. Called from checkXmrBidState, which is coin-B
+        # refund/recovery detection -- so its absence was fund-relevant, not just a
+        # crash on the happy path.
+        #
+        # Built on get_recent_txs_and_info3, the same wallet history call
+        # _getTxUnlockTimes already relies on, rather than a translation of XMR's
+        # incoming_transfers (Zano has no such RPC; see the get_outputs mapping note
+        # in findTxB). Returns the XMRInterface-shaped dict its callers expect, or
+        # None when the tx is absent or not yet buried deep enough.
+        #
+        # NOT YET EXERCISED against a live Zano wallet -- no patched Zano binary
+        # exists on any machine here (see [[zano-patched-wallet-build]]). It is
+        # written to the documented RPC shape and to the idiom of the neighbouring
+        # methods, and it removes a guaranteed AttributeError, but treat its first
+        # live run as unverified.
+        with self._mx_wallet:
+            try:
+                current_height: int = self.getChainHeight()
+            except Exception as e:
+                self._log.info("ZANO getChainHeight failed: %s", str(e))
+                # If the transfer is available it will be deep enough -- same
+                # fallback XMRInterface takes.
+                current_height = None
+
+            try:
+                rv = self.rpc_wallet(
+                    "get_recent_txs_and_info3",
+                    {
+                        "offset": 0,
+                        "count": 1000,
+                        "update_provision_info": False,
+                        "exclude_mining_txs": False,
+                        "exclude_unconfirmed": True,
+                        "order": "FROM_END_TO_BEGIN",
+                    },
+                )
+            except Exception as e:
+                self._log.warning(
+                    "ZANO get_recent_txs_and_info3 failed for {}: {}".format(txid, e)
+                )
+                return None
+
+            for tx in rv.get("transfers", []):
+                if tx.get("tx_hash") != txid:
+                    continue
+                height = tx.get("height", 0)
+                if height in (None, 0):
+                    # Unconfirmed: present in the wallet but not in a block.
+                    return None
+                if (
+                    current_height is not None
+                    and current_height - height <= self.blocks_confirmed
+                ):
+                    return None
+                return {
+                    "txid": tx.get("tx_hash"),
+                    "amount": tx.get("amount", 0),
+                    "height": height,
+                }
+            return None
+
     def getNewRandomKey(self) -> bytes:
         # Note: Returned bytes are in big endian order (same convention xmr.py uses).
         return i2b(9 + secrets.randbelow(ed25519_l - 9))
